 "comment": "App tutorial edit, framed-window layout (ported from start-specwithcode). Each app beat is a list of shots; segments are [srcStart, srcEnd, rate] in take.mp4 (data-media-start = src + syncOffset; syncOffset = blackdetect 2.967 minus black-on cue 3.010); [src, src, 'hold', s|'fit'] holds the frame at src as a still; 'fit' sets the beat's last rate so it fills the beat (refused below minRate, default 0.75; below 0.75 shows a 'Slowed to' badge). aspect is crop width/height; cam keyframes are crop rectangles {src, x, y, w} in source seconds and 1920x1080 pixels (h = w / aspect). Every crop ends on a panel edge (the right panel at x 1462, the thread column 708-1468, the composer top at 918, the settings dialog and its Usage limits card) and scales UI text 1.28x-1.71x. Terminal anchors: [beat, cue|null, offset] or [beat, cue, spokenWord, offset].",
